WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.170
The theory starts from a second-order
Nesterov-Polyak expansion of the loss,

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.242
introducing the input Hessian.

00:00:07.322 --> 00:00:10.764
A zero-mean perturbation cancels first-order terms,

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:17.465
and taking expectations bounds memorization by
expected curvature plus a data-independent offset.

00:00:17.545 --> 00:00:20.504
With the definition of differential privacy,

00:00:20.584 --> 00:00:23.336
a smaller epsilon forces lower curvature.

00:00:23.416 --> 00:00:28.240
Curvature itself is estimated cheaply via
Hutchinson's trace estimator.
